//
// TWO CLOSURES REASSIGNING ONE SCALAR ARE REFUSED (`@FR-L-CapWrite` crossed with
// `@FR-L-CapHeap`).  "Sharing one such variable between TWO closures is refused (a decided
// limit, not a gap); the cure the refusal names is a struct field, which is (L-CapHeap)."  The
// refusal must name that cure.
//
// @EXPECT_ERROR: hold the shared state in a struct field instead
//
// @falsified-at: none — a conformance guard; the refusal fires on 18594597b, interpret and native.
// CHANNEL: the compile diagnostic.
// ARMED: no instrument.
// WITNESS: the diagnostic names the variable and the struct-field cure.
// HOLDS: `two-closures-share-a-struct-field-in-both-directions` beside it.

fn main() {
  n = 1;
  f = fn() { n += 10; };
  g = fn() { n += 100; };
  f();
  g();
  assert(n == 111, "unreachable");
}
